# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Ruins
composer Claude
about    Sandstone halls buried under the mountain: an oboe and its echo in D Phrygian dominant (the flat second and the major third of old temple music) over harp arpeggios, a string pad and a low wordless choir that holds D and A under everything. When something is near, timpani beat twice over a frame drum and a rim; a horn and brass join the fight, a pipe organ and gong come for a guardian.
tempo    70
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.6

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead echo harp drone pad
# mood treasure: harp pad wonder
# mood sense:    timpani bodhran rim drone pad
# mood rise:     sense lead echo harp kick snare
# mood fight:    rise -echo -rim horn brass crash
# mood boss:     fight -lead organ gong

voice lead     oboe      vol=0.55 pan=-0.15 rev=0.5
voice echo     oboe      vol=0.2  pan=0.5  rev=0.7
voice horn     horn      vol=0.62 pan=0.2
voice harp     harp      vol=0.5  pan=0.3
voice drone    voices    vol=0.3  att=1 rel=1.5
voice pad      strings   vol=0.22 pan=-0.25 center=A3 att=0.6 rel=1
voice wonder   musicbox  vol=0.3  pan=0.45 rev=0.7
voice timpani  timpani   vol=0.55 pan=-0.1
voice bodhran  bodhran   vol=0.5  pan=-0.2
voice rim      rim       vol=0.25 pan=0.35
voice kick     kick      vol=0.5
voice snare    snare     vol=0.34 pan=0.1
voice brass    brass     vol=0.36 pan=-0.25 gate=0.8 center=A3
voice crash    crash     vol=0.22 pan=0.2
voice organ    pipe      vol=0.32 att=0.3 rel=0.8
voice gong     gong      vol=0.32 pan=-0.3

# D Eb D Gm | Cm Bb Eb D: the motif with the flat second (D Eb F# A G)
pattern A
lead    | D5------- Eb5--- F#5--- | G5------- Eb5------- | F#5--- Eb5--- D5------- | D5--- Bb4--- G4------- |
lead    | C5--- Eb5--- G5------- | F5------- D5------- | Eb5--- D5--- C5--- Bb4--- | A4----------- .--- |
